Z||000000||MooCow||04-10-2001||08:56 PM||||Well I still have yet to find the cause of the problem on getting my car started.  Parents are now thinking I have to sell it.  So I have till this weekend to get it fixed.  If not I may have to get rid of it.<BR>I have replaced: spark plugs and wires, cap and rotor, ignition modual, coil -up and the coil.  And it still turns over but, doesnt start.  Anyone interested in it let me know.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||9
Z||000001||fiero56||04-10-2001||09:11 PM||||Ken, are you sure you don't have spark, or are you just asusming that is the problem. Are the rockers moving when you crank the engine?||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||04-10-2001||09:16 PM||||What are the rockers??  I know that the belts turn over.  And I can make the engine turn over as many times as I wish, but have yet to do that cause I dont want to fludd it.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000003||Songman||04-10-2001||09:23 PM||||Ken,<P>Not sure on a 3.4 but on my 4 cyl. all I had to do was take the oil filler cap off and look down inside the valve cover while I had my girlfriend crank the engine over.<P>Unfortunately, I saw no movement when she cranked it. This means broken cam gear. That is why my 88 coupe has been sitting since the day after Christmas.<P>It is not an expensive thing to fix, but it is a fairly involved thing to fix. And I'd say the 3.4 probably has a timing chain or belt. Try the oil filler cap thing and see if you can see rocker arms. Rocker arms are like pivots. You'll recognize them if they are visible. If they move, your problem is elsewhere. If not, well, at least you know.<P>As much as I hate to say it, that does sound like your problem...<P>Let us know...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||jaguiler||04-10-2001||09:30 PM||||My GT when I got it would not start for about 15 minutes the morning after i braught it home.  Once I got it up I tool it straight to a cheap tuneup place.  They did an engine diagnostic.  $60.  And they told me the problem.. It was the TPS sensor.  Maybe you can try getting the codes for the ECM, right below the plate that holds your cig. lighter and test to find out what it is.  Probably a sensor....hopefully....<P>Good luck...don't give up yet...try what I said....it worked great for me!<P><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||04-10-2001||09:44 PM||||Thanks guys.  Now that I am off of work till next week I can hopefully fix my car.  I will try what you said but the bad thing is that I only have like $150 to fix the problem.  After that I am back to broke.  I will let you know how it goes tomorrow.  Any other ideas?  Keep them comming.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
