Z||000007||Fformula88||04-10-2001||10:17 PM||||Try taking the wire off of the distributor cap that comes from the coil.  Brace it near something metal on the engine so it will jump to ground and watch it while someone cranks the car.  This will tell you if your getting spark or not.  It sounds like its not getting spark or fuel.<P>Other components to check are the distributor itself, the fuel pump (no fuel, no start  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Also be sure there is gas in it!!  I had the car start to run bad on my way to somebody's house.  When I went to leave it wouldn't start... I was empty!  Darn faulty gas guage!) Good luck, and keep us posted!  Whatever you do, don't get rid of this car for this problem.  Even if you have it towed to a garage and pay a hundred bucks for diagnosis, its a lot cheaper than a new car!  Especially with all the work you've got into this one!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
