Z||000013||ferg||04-11-2001||01:44 PM||||I see that you have a 3.4- is that the 3.4 that came out of a camaro? Or is it the 3.4 with dual overhead cams?<P>Reason being is that the dual over head cam 3.4's are somewhat notorious for breaking the timing belt. This happened to a friend of mine who had approx. 80,000 miles on the engine. I have another friend who's car did the same thing around the same mileage.<P>Have you tried starting fluid to see if it will fire when you crank it? If it starts temporarily then you have fuel issues, if it doesn't run then you have spark issues. Something to try at least.<P>I don't know if that helps- but good luck with it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||MooCow||04-11-2001||02:48 PM||||Okay I went out today and moved it in the garage to work on my Fiero.  I did the codes and got 2 codes.  The first one was code 13 which is the oxygen sensor.  The second code I got was code 24 which says it can only be detected while the vehicle is moving and to disrecard it.  Looks like now I can keep.<BR>Hey ferg I have 95 camaro engine not the DOHC one.  I am calling Ed tomorrow if I can't fix it today.  I will let you know what happens.<P>Thanks Ken<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||MooCow||04-11-2001||04:06 PM||||K I now have no spark at all.  I do have fuel comming in cause I can smell it when i try to start it, but no spark.  I changed everything and till nothing. So I am going to go through it again.  I also got a hanes manual for my Birthday today so I  am going throught that as well.  Anyone know what to check for??<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||2
Z||000016||Indiana_resto_guy||04-11-2001||04:56 PM||||Are you calling the pick-up coil this 'coil -up'?<BR>If it is, I know that in the 2.8 that you need to remove the distributor to replace it. Did you get the distributor back in correctly?<BR>Check for +12 volts to the coil, This is the main feed for the HIE circut. Without those volts to the coil, you get no spark. I wish I was more familar with your engine. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||stsmithgt||04-11-2001||05:14 PM||||Getting the command to sell your car is nothing new when you live with parents.  I was forced to do that back in 79' after sinking MY EARNED $1000.00 bucks into a chevy I <I>had</I>.  I had to sell it in two weeks because I was putting too much money into it.  What are kids supposed to do with money?  I was able to get 200.00 for it. THAT Hanes manual should act as a coupon to extend any sale dead line.  You have to get some use out of the book, and that takes time. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> GOOD LUCK!||||reg||1
